From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 16:41:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998: put the GPU clock controller in
 VDD_MX

The GPU's memories sit on VDD_MX, which it shares with the display
controller, and its registers sit behind GPU_GX_GDSC. Those two are voted by
unrelated devices: the GPU node names VDD_MX, while the SMMU node holds
GPU_GX_GDSC purely to bring up its parent GPU_CX_GDSC -- the DTS says so
itself. Nothing orders them.

So on a display blank the GPU's runtime suspend drops the MX vote while the
SMMU is still lingering on its 20 ms autosuspend with GX up. A transaction
into the GPU in that window answers to nobody and the SoC takes a watchdog
reset. It reproduces on roughly one wake in twenty: a power-key cycler that
counts only real panel transitions died at cycle 45, silently, with nothing
on any console.

Naming VDD_MX on the clock controller makes gdsc_register() add each of its
GDSCs as a subdomain of it, giving mx -> gpu_cx -> gpu_gx. genpd then powers
MX on before GX and refuses to drop it while GX is on, which is the
invariant the hardware wanted all along.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
index a7b737389fd1..8de03f229509 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998.dtsi
@@ -2674,6 +2674,22 @@ gpucc: clock-controller@5065000 {
 				 <&gcc GCC_GPU_GPLL0_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "xo",
 				      "gpll0";
+
+			/*
+			 * The GPU's memories are on VDD_MX, which it shares
+			 * with the display. Without this the two are voted by
+			 * unrelated devices -- the GPU node votes MX, the SMMU
+			 * node holds GPU_GX_GDSC -- so nothing orders them, and
+			 * on a display blank MX drops to level 0 while GX is
+			 * still up. A transaction into the GPU then answers to
+			 * nobody and the SoC takes a watchdog reset.
+			 *
+			 * Naming MX here makes gdsc_register() add every GDSC
+			 * in this controller as a subdomain of it, so genpd
+			 * powers MX on before GPU_CX/GPU_GX and refuses to drop
+			 * it while either is on.
+			 */
+			power-domains = <&rpmpd MSM8998_VDDMX>;
 		};
 
 		lpass_q6_smmu: iommu@5100000 {
